-- title:
--   At a candidate u, under Roy's strong six exponentials theorem, a rational function z of u whose conjugation hull meets Theorem F's criterion is not in ℒ̃
-- statement:
--   Here $\mathcal{L}$ is the set of logarithms of algebraic numbers (the $z \in \mathbb{C}$ with $e^z$ algebraic), and $\widetilde{\mathcal{L}}$ is the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-vector space spanned by $1$ and $\mathcal{L}$; spans and linear independence are over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the algebraic numbers. Roy's strong six exponentials theorem is carried as the hypothesis `hSSE`: if $x_1, x_2 \in \mathbb{C}$ are linearly independent and so are $y_1, y_2, y_3 \in \mathbb{C}$, then one of the six products $x_iy_j$ is not in $\widetilde{\mathcal{L}}$.
--
--   Let $u$ be a candidate for Diaz's conjecture (`DiazModulus.IsCandidate`: $u \neq 0$, with $|u|$ and $e^u$ algebraic), let $z$ lie in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}(u)$, the subfield of $\mathbb{C}$ generated by $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $u$, and let $W_z = \mathrm{span}(1, u, \bar u, z, \bar z)$, the conjugation hull of $z$. Suppose $W_z$ meets Theorem F's criterion, that is, one of the following holds:
--
--   - $\dim W_z = 4$, and $z \in \mathrm{span}(1, u, \bar u, (u - a)^{-1})$ for some $a \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $a\bar a = u\bar u$;
--   - $\dim W_z = 5$, and $W_z$ satisfies (D1), (D2a) or (D2b) below.
--
--   Here, with $W = W_z$:
--
--   - **(D1)** there are linearly independent $t_0, t_1, t_2 \in \mathbb{C}$ with $t_j \in W$ and $ut_j \in W$ for every $j$;
--   - **(D2a, two-orbit)** $W = \mathrm{span}(1, u, u^{-1}, Q'(u)S_1(u)/(uP'(u)), P'(u)S_2(u)/(uQ'(u)))$ for some $P', Q', S_1, S_2 \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}[X]$ with $P', Q'$ coprime, $\max(\deg P', \deg Q') = 2$ and $\deg S_1, \deg S_2 \leq 2$;
--   - **(D2b, cyclic)** $W = \mathrm{span}(1, u, u^{-1}, Q'(u)S_1(u)/(uP'(u)), Q'(u)(Q'(u)S_1(u) + P'(u)S_2(u))/(uP'(u)^2))$ for some such $P', Q', S_1, S_2$.
--
--   Then $z \notin \widetilde{\mathcal{L}}$.
--
--   **Proof.** By Hermite–Lindemann (`DiazModulus.hermite_lindemann_holds`, 3.2), $u \notin \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, since $u \neq 0$ and $e^u$ is algebraic; and $u\bar u = |u|^2$ is algebraic, as $|u|$ is. So Theorem F (`DiazModulus.rational_conj_hull_two_by_three_configuration_iff`, 10.146) applies to $z \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}(u)$, and its “if” direction puts a $2 \times 3$ configuration in $W_z$. If $z \in \widetilde{\mathcal{L}}$, then $W_z \subseteq \widetilde{\mathcal{L}}$: $1 \in \widetilde{\mathcal{L}}$, $u \in \mathcal{L}$ since $e^u$ is algebraic, $\bar u \in \mathcal{L}$ (`DiazModulus.logAlg_conj_stable`) and $\bar z \in \widetilde{\mathcal{L}}$ (`DiazModulus.logAlgTilde_conj_stable`). The configuration then lies in $\widetilde{\mathcal{L}}$, against `hSSE`.
--
--   **Novelty.** Not found in the sources read as a family; routine. Its content is the “if” direction of Theorem F (`DiazModulus.rational_conj_hull_two_by_three_configuration_iff`): with a configuration in $W_z$ as the hypothesis instead of Theorem F's criterion, the conclusion holds for every $z \in \mathbb{C}$, and Theorem F is not needed. Each instance is a substitution in Roy's strong six exponentials theorem (Roy 1992, Cor. 2), as in `DiazModulus.candidate_laurent_conj_hull_class_not_mem_logAlgTilde` (10.106) for Theorem E's classes. Special cases are printed configurations: in dimension 4, Diaz's Théorème 7(1) (2007) at $v = 1/(u - a)$, with the exclusion in its Corollaire 5(4); for polynomials of degree 2 and 3 in $u$, Théorème 7(1); and Theorem E's class (Q) is a substitution in Diaz's Théorème 2 (2004) and Théorème 4(1) (2007). It concerns candidates, so it is vacuous if Diaz's conjecture holds.
-- source:
--   Not found in the sources read as a family. Each instance is a substitution in Roy's strong six exponentials theorem (D. Roy, Matrices whose coefficients are linear forms in logarithms, J. Number Theory 41 (1992), 22–47, Cor. 2), which is carried as a hypothesis; the content is the “if” direction of Theorem F (DiazModulus.rational_conj_hull_two_by_three_configuration_iff, 10.146), in the pattern of DiazModulus.candidate_laurent_conj_hull_class_not_mem_logAlgTilde (10.106) for Theorem E's classes. Special cases are printed: in dimension 4 the configuration is G. Diaz, Produits et quotients de combinaisons linéaires de logarithmes de nombres algébriques : conjectures et résultats partiels, J. Théor. Nombres Bordeaux 19 (2007), 373–391, Théorème 7(1) at v = 1/(u − a), with the exclusion in its Corollaire 5(4); for polynomials of degree 2 and 3 in u it is Théorème 7(1); Theorem E's class (Q) is a substitution in G. Diaz, Utilisation de la conjugaison complexe dans l'étude de la transcendance de valeurs de la fonction exponentielle usuelle, J. Théor. Nombres Bordeaux 16 (2004), 535–553, Théorème 2, and in Diaz 2007, Théorème 4(1). Uses DiazModulus.rational_conj_hull_two_by_three_configuration_iff, DiazModulus.hermite_lindemann_holds, DiazModulus.logAlg_conj_stable and DiazModulus.logAlgTilde_conj_stable. R21a of the Diaz modulus mission. Formal proof: Diaz modulus mission, 23 October 2026 (C. Perassi).

import Definitions.Def_DiazModulus

open Complex ComplexConjugate

namespace DiazModulus

open Polynomial in
theorem candidate_rational_conj_hull_criterion_not_mem_logAlgTilde
    (hSSE : ∀ (x : Fin 2 → ℂ) (y : Fin 3 → ℂ),
      LinearIndependent (↥Qbar) x → LinearIndependent (↥Qbar) y →
      ¬ (∀ i j, x i * y j ∈ LogAlgTilde))
    (u z : ℂ) (hcand : IsCandidate u) (hz : z ∈ IntermediateField.adjoin Qbar ({u} : Set ℂ))
    (hF : (Module.finrank (↥Qbar) (Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, conj u, z, conj z} : Set ℂ)) = 4 ∧ ∃ a ∈ Qbar, a * conj a = u * conj u ∧
          z ∈ Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, conj u, (u - a)⁻¹} : Set ℂ)) ∨
      (Module.finrank (↥Qbar) (Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, conj u, z, conj z} : Set ℂ)) = 5 ∧
        ((∃ t : Fin 3 → ℂ, LinearIndependent (↥Qbar) t ∧ ∀ j, t j ∈ Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, conj u, z, conj z} : Set ℂ) ∧ u * t j ∈ Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, conj u, z, conj z} : Set ℂ)) ∨ (∃ P' Q' S₁ S₂ : (↥Qbar)[X], IsCoprime P' Q' ∧ max P'.natDegree Q'.natDegree = 2 ∧
        S₁.natDegree ≤ 2 ∧ S₂.natDegree ≤ 2 ∧
        Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, conj u, z, conj z} : Set ℂ) = Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, u⁻¹, aeval u Q' * aeval u S₁ / (u * aeval u P'),
          aeval u P' * aeval u S₂ / (u * aeval u Q')} : Set ℂ)) ∨
        (∃ P' Q' S₁ S₂ : (↥Qbar)[X], IsCoprime P' Q' ∧ max P'.natDegree Q'.natDegree = 2 ∧
        S₁.natDegree ≤ 2 ∧ S₂.natDegree ≤ 2 ∧
        Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, conj u, z, conj z} : Set ℂ) = Submodule.span Qbar ({1, u, u⁻¹, aeval u Q' * aeval u S₁ / (u * aeval u P'),
          aeval u Q' * (aeval u Q' * aeval u S₁ + aeval u P' * aeval u S₂) / (u * aeval u P' ^ 2)} :
            Set ℂ))))) :
    z ∉ LogAlgTilde := by
  sorry

end DiazModulus
